   For an Abel/geometric tail bound we would need |Λ_k| <= C g^k with g<1.
   Observed: Λ_k do NOT decay geometrically — they plateau / decay sub-geometrically,
   and even sum|prod s| per level DIVERGES (k>=3). A Polya–Vinogradov per-level bound
   |Σ_{|T|=k} ∏ s| <= G^k is FALSE as stated (the unsigned mass is unbounded);
   only the SIGNED, symmetric-limit Λ_k is finite, which no elementary summation
   method can certify a lower bound from below.

DONE.
